From b65bc1d9c2e4920a2561e90858bdb8bc2b2e235a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:07:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: lay out fixed-mode tables like Blink, and apply
 column-group widths

Fixed mode gets its own column measures and width distribution, modelled
on Blink's DistributeInlineSizeToComputedInlineSizeFixed: a col width
beats the first-row cell's, a colspan cell gives each spanned column an
equal share minus spacing, auto columns split what is left, and with no
auto columns the extra goes to fixed columns in proportion, or else to
percentage columns. A colgroup's width applies to its auto-width cols in
auto mode; before, a colspan cell gave all its width to one column and a
width on a colgroup produced 0-width columns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/layout/table/layout.rs | 195 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 189 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

